      "chapter",
      1,
      "Part 1: AI Superpowers and the Empirical Verification Gauntlet",
      "Unleashes the raw capability claims of BEJSON (Boehnen Elton JSON) and MFDB (Multi-File Database) framed as empirical AI superpowers, contrasting sub-50MB flat-file efficiency against bloated enterprise database daemons. Provides battle-tested verification prompt templates designed to challenge frontier LLMs (Large Language Models) to independently audit and verify token reduction, 80x lookup speedups, and zero-hallucination mechanics. Transitions directly into the structural evolution of the specification from its foundational beginnings to the current production standard.",
