      "chapter",
      3,
      "Part 3: Positional Field Separation, Matrix Layouts, and Token Economics",
      "Dissects the mechanics of positional field access, explaining how decoupling schema metadata in the Fields array from row vectors in the Values array eliminates key repetition and token bloat. Explains how deterministic array indexing prevents key-spelling hallucinations while maintaining constant-time field lookups via the in-memory field-map cache. Establishes how these single-file layout optimizations scale into coordinated, multi-table systems governed by relational invariants.",
      null,
      "planned",
